# Parameters consumed via `-lib boring` (comments only; haxelib strips these lines).
#
# Defines (documented for `haxe --help-defines` via defines.json):
#   runtime-import, runtime-emit, ts-output, kotlin-output, rust-output,
#   float-precision (f64 default, f32 per feature spec 23)
#
# Macro entry points (on the package class path `src`):
#   --macro Intercept.run(<sourceDirs>, <excludedFiles>)
#   plus exactly one target activation:
#   --macro tscompiler.Compiler.use()
#   --macro kotlincompiler.Compiler.use()
#   --macro rustcompiler.Compiler.use()
#
# Target compilers sit below `src` at non-package-aligned depth and cannot ride
# the package class path; add them per compilation, as examples/*.hxml do:
#   -cp <boring>/src/reflaxe/<target>/std-shadow
#   -cp <boring>/src/reflaxe/<target>
